<title>USA: Stanley to buy back shares from fund.</title>
<headline>Stanley to buy back shares from fund.</headline>
<dateline>STANLEYTOWN, Va. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stanley Furniture Co Inc said on Tuesday that its board approved the repurchase of 750,000 common shares from the M.L. Lee Acquisition Fund for $20 a share.</p>
<p>The deal, which is expected to close by June 30, 1997, will cut the fund's stake to 22 percent from 34 percent and would have added about $0.06 a share to earnings on a proforma basis for its March quarter.</p>
<p>Funding for the $15 million repurchase will come from available cash and its existing bank credit facility, Stanley Furniture said in a statement.</p>
</text>
